12. What Would Make SIE Unnecessary?

SIE should be tested adversarially. The following protocol should be used.

12.1 Adversarial LLM Protocol

Multiple independent LLM research agents should be instructed to answer:

“Why should SIE not exist?”

They should be forced to compare SIE directly with:

· dyadic completion
· moralization
· theory of mind / agency detection
· psychological essentialism
· myth of pure evil
· demonization
· dehumanization
· moral disengagement
· minimally counterintuitive concepts
· cultural evolution of moralizing gods
· Belief in Pure Evil / Belief in Pure Good
· Govrin’s prototype model of evil perception
· rate–distortion–perception frameworks

Then they should answer:

“What empirical observation would make SIE unnecessary?”

12.2 Possible Outcomes

If several independent LLMs conclude:

“SIE is only a descriptive combination of known mechanisms and makes no differential predictions.”

then SIE should be abandoned.

If they find:

“The mechanisms exist separately, but no existing theory predicts their recursive composition, their cultural feedback loop, or the compression–distortion trade-off at the cultural level.”

then SIE has earned its place.

